From c2bc256933a6108d68cbce258813e4479a7f6ef4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kfir adler <kfira@checkpoint.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 17:48:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add neon hover theme, clearer scanner favorites, richer
 lookup, TradingView links

- Theme: green neon hover system (tokens, .link-hover, nav/table/selection),
  bright neon in dark, readable deep green in light. Applied to nav, result
  symbols, sortable headers, breadcrumbs, similar-stocks links.
- Scanner: consolidated favorites/saved into one prominent star card with
  one-tap load, plus a top-bar favorite loader; added section hints so editing
  filters is clearer; removed duplicate quick-actions block.
- Scanner results: clicking a symbol opens the correct TradingView page,
  letting TradingView resolve NASDAQ/NYSE (and handling TASE), in a new tab.
- Lookup: replaced dev-facing coverage diagnostics with a meaningful Key
  levels & metrics panel (SMA distances, 60-bar range position, ATR/volatility,
  band proximity, sequence/break context); kept coverage gaps as a slim note.
- Fix: TechnicalSummaryPanel showed ATR% 100x too small.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
